# State describes live infrastructure and can contain resource contents; plans
# can contain variable values. Neither belongs in a repository, and no backend
# is configured here precisely so that nobody acquires shared state by
# accident.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately absent from this list: the dependency
# lock pins provider hashes and belongs in the repository. It appears on the
# first `terraform init`, which has not been run here because no Terraform
# binary was available in this environment.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log

# Real values live outside the repository. The example file is tracked.
*.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example
